Currently, eating a Quantum Mechanic makes your speed "uncertain", and
toggles it between fast & slow.  This is based on the fact that quantum
states that it's impossible to know both a particle's exact position
and its exact velocity.

Of course, this means that you always know where you are when you eat a
Q corpse.  Seems like some of the time (50%?), you should instead know
how fast you're going--and thus end up doing a [controlled] teleport.

And, by extension: make it so that Q attacks can your intrinsic speed
some of the time, in addition to their chance to change your position.
They should never be able to change both at the same time, of course.

(And yes, this thought struck me when my wizard killed a Q down in the
mines and immediately ate the corpse, since it was a no-risk way to get
intrinsic speed...)

